  <h2>Current Minimum Wage Rates Across Canada</h2>
  <p>
    Minimum wage in Canada is set independently by each province and territory, with a separate federal rate
    that applies to federally regulated industries such as banking, telecommunications, interprovincial
    transportation, and the postal service. As of 2025, provincial minimum wages range from $15.00 per hour
    in Alberta to $19.00 per hour in Nunavut, reflecting significant regional differences in the cost of
    living and labour market conditions.
  </p>
  <p>
    Most provinces adjust their minimum wage annually on either January 1 or October 1, often tying increases
    to the Consumer Price Index (CPI) to keep pace with inflation. Understanding these rates is essential for
    both workers and employers to ensure compliance with employment standards legislation.
  </p>

