  <h2>Minimum Wage and Take-Home Pay</h2>
  <p>
    Earning minimum wage does not mean you take home the full amount. Federal and provincial income taxes,
    CPP contributions, and EI premiums are deducted from every paycheque. For example, a full-time minimum
    wage worker in Ontario earning $17.20 per hour ($35,776 annually) would take home approximately $31,200
    after deductions, depending on their personal tax credits and province of residence. Use our
    <a href="/">salary calculator</a> to estimate your exact take-home pay at any wage rate.
  </p>

